# Prompts tokenized with Python's lock released where the recipe's 0099 does not reach, and 0099's calls made safe for
# a tokenizer without the batch call. The Rust tokenizer's single-text encode holds the GIL for the whole text, so
# while a prompt is tokenized no other thread of the engine process runs, the decode loop of every other request
# included. The recipe's 0099 moved the server's prompts, /tokenize and a picture request's layout to
# encode_batch_fast; this patch does the same for the two calls it does not cover, through tensorfold/cuda/unlocked.py
# (encode_batch_fast, encode_batch before tokenizers 0.20): the media markers' template (tensorfold/cuda/markers.py)
# and 9005's new part of a resumed conversation (resume.py). 0099's two calls (App._encode_ids, GlmVision.prepare) go
# through the same helper, which asks a tokenizer without a batch call with encode: the same ids from the real
# tokenizer, and TensorFold's own tests, whose stand-in tokenizers have only encode, run against the tree again.
# mgllm, 2026-10-08; narrowed to what 0099 does not cover and 0099's calls made safe, 2026-10-10.
# Tests: tests/test_9006_unlocked_tokenize.py (CPU; needs TF_GLM_TEST_MODEL_DIR).

